WEBVTT

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:15.360
"I can't overcome it"  "I'm annoyed"

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:20.100
Even if I break down those hurdles

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:28.310
No answer emerges

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:34.810
Am I being controlled?  Everyone on the field

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:39.750
Isn't scared, go away, but...

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:43.450
The unseen road to the future

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:51.200
Cannot be chosen

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:54.500
Close your eyes and cut with your heart

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:58.160
just like cards, surely

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:03.230
It was promised  yes!  you are the winner

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:06.100
never lose!  Cut with your heart

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.330
just like cards, surely

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:16.680
Because a miracle will occur

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:28.500
The Legendary Fisherman

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:45.770
Jonouchi, Kajiki has no monsters on his field!

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:46.820
Now's your chance!

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:49.490
I know, but...

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:55.330
In his Umi ocean field, I can't attack him carelessly.

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:57.080
I draw a card!

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:04.620
What will you do, Jonouchi?

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:07.200
Are you brave enough to attack in the ocean?

00:02:10.210 --> 00:02:11.640
Here I go!  My turn!

00:02:12.350 --> 00:02:14.510
Baby Dragon in attack position.

00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:19.890
I get it.  You're going to use it to test the waters.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:22.420
No, Kajiki.

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:24.560
I play Polymerization.

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:32.260
It levels up into Alligator's Sword Dragon!

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:37.870
You chose to increase its attack points instead of attacking.

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:43.400
According to Battle City rules, Fusion Monsters can't attack on the turn that they're summoned.

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:44.810
I end my turn.

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:47.620
Then it's my turn.

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:49.220
I draw a card!

00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:52.220
I summon a monster to the field!

00:02:54.970 --> 00:02:56.820
He played a monster card?

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:00.130
I end my turn!

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:03.830
Kajiki is controlling the ocean.

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:04.560
Yeah.

00:03:04.770 --> 00:03:06.250
What card did he play?

00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:10.500
I don't even know if it's in attack or defense position.  However...

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:12.700
What's wrong, Jonouchi?

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:14.170
Cross these waters!

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:18.950
I don't know what card you played.

00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:22.850
But it's definitely a Water Attribute monster.

00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:25.150
What?

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:28.490
Go, Alligator's Sword Dragon!

00:03:28.490 --> 00:03:33.840
It can fly over Water Attribute monsters to attack you directly!

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:36.030
Glide Sword!

00:03:40.890 --> 00:03:42.090
Oh yeah!

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:45.700
I've overcome your Umi ocean field!

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:49.030
The ocean...

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:03.820
You did it, Dad!

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:08.160
Dad, look!

00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:15.030
Don't underestimate the ocean!

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:16.230
My turn!

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:18.840
I set a card and end my turn!

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:20.660
Another card?

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:24.000
But Kajiki, the duel is already over.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:24.880
My turn!

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:26.910
I set a card.

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:29.140
Fly, Alligator's Sword Dragon!

00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:32.540
If this direct attack succeeds...

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:33.920
Jonouchi wins.

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:36.390
Go!  Attack him directly!

00:04:36.890 --> 00:04:39.060
Kajiki will have 0 life points!

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:41.560
It won't be that easy!

00:04:41.890 --> 00:04:45.740
I activate the Continuous Trap Tornado Wall!

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:51.600
What?

00:04:55.600 --> 00:05:01.510
As long as I have Tornado Wall on the Umi field, you can't attack me directly.

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:05.370
Wait a sec.

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:10.390
He lifted all the water into the air to create Tornado Wall.

00:05:10.730 --> 00:05:13.800
But I don't see his monster.

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:15.020
That's strange.

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:18.760
Maybe Kajiki didn't summon a monster.

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:24.200
It seems you can't see my monster, Jonouchi.

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:26.940
I end my turn.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:30.960
My turn.

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:35.180
I tribute the monster on my field to summon another monster.

00:05:40.050 --> 00:05:44.560
Tribute?  So he did have a monster!

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:51.500
Here I go, Jonouchi!

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:54.860
Where's the attack going to come from?

00:05:58.820 --> 00:06:01.000
Go!  Sea Stealth II!

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:02.340
The Legendary Fisherman!

00:06:09.150 --> 00:06:11.650
The Quick-Play Spell Energy Drain!

00:06:12.550 --> 00:06:16.370
I draw a card, and your monster's attack points drop to 0!

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:20.550
It won't work!

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:26.370
No way!  My Alligator's Sword Dragon!

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:27.030
Why?

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:36.470
As long as Umi is on the field, you can't attack or use spells on The Legendary Fisherman.

00:06:36.470 --> 00:06:38.190
What?

00:06:39.160 --> 00:06:42.860
The Legendary Fisherman knows everything about the ocean.

00:06:43.050 --> 00:06:45.480
There's no way you can destroy it.

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:49.420
My turn.  I draw a card.

00:06:49.820 --> 00:06:54.360
I set a monster in defense position and end my turn.

00:06:54.730 --> 00:06:55.730
My turn.

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:57.770
I summon a monster.

00:06:58.120 --> 00:06:58.800
Attack!

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:02.520
Where will it attack from?

00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:09.520
Little-Winguard!

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:15.600
Jonouchi, you don't know where you were attacked from.

00:07:16.070 --> 00:07:20.820
The dangers of the ocean where hidden monsters dwell.  This is Sea Stealth II!

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:22.660
Look.

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:31.400
What's this monster?

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:33.900
It looks like a real human.

00:07:34.770 --> 00:07:37.830
Jonouchi, that card is alive.

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:40.630
That card is my dad's double.

00:07:40.630 --> 00:07:43.400
You won't defeat him easily.

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:45.000
Your dad's double?

00:07:45.130 --> 00:07:46.400
That's right.

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:51.550
That card was sent to me three years after my dad vanished in the seas.

00:08:04.060 --> 00:08:04.930
Dad?

00:08:05.690 --> 00:08:08.570
Dad?

00:08:08.770 --> 00:08:11.030
Dad!

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:17.850
My dad was never found, and we built his grave on a cliff.

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:21.580
It was his final request.

00:08:22.300 --> 00:08:27.400
If anything happened to him, he wanted his grave to overlook the ocean.

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:34.670
Since the day he disappeared, I visited his grave everyday.

00:08:35.150 --> 00:08:40.200
I didn't go to pay my respects.  Just the opposite.

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:47.140
I thought that he'd come home yelling, “How dare you build my grave!"

00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:52.400
Ryota!  You won't believe it!

00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:55.750
You got a letter from your dad!

00:08:56.050 --> 00:08:57.200
What?

00:09:00.450 --> 00:09:02.920
It was my dad's handwriting.

00:09:03.370 --> 00:09:05.850
"Ryota this is a man's card."

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:07.670
"Use it to win!"

00:09:10.470 --> 00:09:11.750
My dad is...

00:09:11.750 --> 00:09:14.230
My dad is alive!

00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:24.710
I only found out later that before he vanished, my dad asked his friend to get the card for me.

00:09:25.150 --> 00:09:28.040
And it arrived after many months.

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:32.480
It was only for a second, but this card showed me a miracle.

00:09:32.740 --> 00:09:35.940
My dad's soul lives inside this card!

00:09:36.110 --> 00:09:38.280
That's what I believe.

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:41.770
That's why you won't defeat it easily!

00:09:43.480 --> 00:09:44.540
Kajiki...

00:09:44.540 --> 00:09:47.430
It's your turn, Jonouchi!

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:49.100
I draw a card.

00:09:49.570 --> 00:09:54.370
I can feel The Legendary Fisherman watching me.

00:09:54.920 --> 00:09:57.370
Can I really destroy that monster?

00:09:58.050 --> 00:10:00.200
I set a card!

00:10:01.230 --> 00:10:03.750
And a monster in defense position.

00:10:04.300 --> 00:10:05.680
I end my turn.

00:10:05.960 --> 00:10:10.350
You're trying to elude me, but there's nowhere you can go.

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:13.060
And the ocean is even more terrifying!

00:10:13.360 --> 00:10:14.760
My turn!

00:10:15.370 --> 00:10:17.030
Fortress Whale's Oath!

00:10:17.230 --> 00:10:20.840
I tribute monsters that total Level 7.

00:10:25.050 --> 00:10:27.140
Come out, the guardian of the seas!

00:10:28.700 --> 00:10:30.860
Surface, Fortress Whale!

00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:38.180
What?

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:44.760
Jonouchi, you're finished!

00:11:12.410 --> 00:11:13.620
Forget it.

00:11:14.580 --> 00:11:15.750
What's wrong?

00:11:15.750 --> 00:11:20.120
I know I won't lose to you, but we share a common interest.

00:11:20.520 --> 00:11:21.650
Right?

00:11:22.770 --> 00:11:24.660
You made a wise decision.

00:11:25.310 --> 00:11:30.400
If you want Yugi, it's quicker if you go after his friends instead.

00:11:30.840 --> 00:11:33.620
I'm waiting for my chance.

00:11:33.820 --> 00:11:39.300
That's what I'm planning to do with the power of my Millennium Rod.

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:41.580
But their bond is strong.

00:11:42.100 --> 00:11:44.250
You won't break it easily.

00:11:44.450 --> 00:11:49.420
That's why having Bakura to host me is useful.

00:11:49.570 --> 00:11:50.970
A host?

00:11:51.280 --> 00:11:52.850
How interesting.

00:11:54.280 --> 00:11:55.020
I can...

00:11:55.580 --> 00:11:57.060
...use him.

00:12:00.640 --> 00:12:03.040
I summon Fortress Whale!

00:12:03.400 --> 00:12:06.470
The Umi field powers it up!

00:12:06.760 --> 00:12:08.900
How am I supposed to destroy that?

00:12:09.300 --> 00:12:13.580
Jonouchi, you'll learn how scary the ocean is.

00:12:13.820 --> 00:12:16.350
The Legendary Fisherman, attack!

00:12:17.680 --> 00:12:20.120
You have no more defending monsters!

00:12:21.140 --> 00:12:22.920
Get ready, Jonouchi!

00:12:23.320 --> 00:12:24.520
Oh no!

00:12:24.700 --> 00:12:27.250
Fire!  Whale Bombard!

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:31.500
No!

00:12:31.500 --> 00:12:32.570
Jonouchi!

00:12:34.670 --> 00:12:37.200
That big whale is gonna end this!

00:12:37.200 --> 00:12:39.070
That showoff duelist will lose!

00:12:39.420 --> 00:12:42.870
Jonouchi, don't give up!

00:12:42.870 --> 00:12:46.850
You're going to win this duel and battle Yugi again, right?

00:12:46.850 --> 00:12:48.700
I know.

00:12:48.700 --> 00:12:53.850
But The Legendary Fisherman will destroy my monsters instantly.

00:12:53.850 --> 00:12:56.790
And I don't know when I should play my trap.

00:12:57.060 --> 00:13:01.130
If nothing changes, Kajiki will win on his next turn.

00:13:02.100 --> 00:13:06.130
Jonouchi must find The Legendary Fisherman's location before then.

00:13:06.130 --> 00:13:07.760
But where is it?

00:13:09.250 --> 00:13:10.470
What's up?

00:13:10.620 --> 00:13:14.570
I think I saw two shadows in the pool.

00:13:14.800 --> 00:13:16.680
What's the holdup, Jonouchi?

00:13:16.680 --> 00:13:18.010
It's your turn.

00:13:18.350 --> 00:13:21.680
Fortress Whale above and The Legendary Fisherman below.

00:13:22.050 --> 00:13:23.170
Will I lose?

00:13:25.920 --> 00:13:28.270
There's real water behind me?

00:13:28.270 --> 00:13:30.800
I couldn't tell because of the Umi field-

00:13:34.710 --> 00:13:37.660
I know where The Legendary Fisherman is!

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:39.090
My turn!

00:13:39.820 --> 00:13:44.800
I have two spells, one monster and one trap in my hand.

00:13:45.240 --> 00:13:47.600
And one set card on the field.

00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:50.200
My back is against the wall.

00:13:50.200 --> 00:13:52.410
I have to take a chance!

00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:56.010
I set two cards on the field.

00:13:56.010 --> 00:13:59.650
And I summon Panther Warrior in attack position!

00:14:02.600 --> 00:14:06.250
Panther Warrior requires a tribute to attack.

00:14:06.250 --> 00:14:08.360
It can't do anything alone.

00:14:08.560 --> 00:14:10.460
I end my turn.

00:14:10.730 --> 00:14:13.420
This'll be my final turn!

00:14:13.420 --> 00:14:15.160
I'll finish you quick!

00:14:15.510 --> 00:14:18.600
If my guess is wrong, I lose.

00:14:20.600 --> 00:14:21.560
One!

00:14:22.370 --> 00:14:24.180
Fortress Whale attacks!

00:14:24.180 --> 00:14:25.760
Whale Bombard!

00:14:28.340 --> 00:14:30.960
There it is!  I reveal my trap card!

00:14:30.960 --> 00:14:33.060
Magic-Arm Shield!

00:14:35.820 --> 00:14:38.380
I found you, The Legendary Fisherman!

00:14:38.530 --> 00:14:40.390
You're over there!

00:14:43.350 --> 00:14:49.800
The Umi field overlaps with the pool, so that's where you hid your monster.

00:14:50.010 --> 00:14:52.230
You figured out my Sea Stealth strategy?

00:14:54.300 --> 00:14:57.120
Fortress Whale's attack doesn't stop!

00:14:57.120 --> 00:15:01.280
It targets The Legendary Fisherman instead of Panther Warrior!

00:15:01.630 --> 00:15:02.710
Fisherman!

00:15:21.360 --> 00:15:25.290
It's over.  I lost this duel.

00:15:25.290 --> 00:15:26.770
What do you mean?

00:15:26.960 --> 00:15:32.210
Since The Legendary Fisherman is gone, it's over for me.

00:15:32.210 --> 00:15:35.960
Whatever!  You still have Fortress Whale.

00:15:35.960 --> 00:15:39.530
And you have more life points than me!

00:15:39.530 --> 00:15:44.880
No.  I've always fought alongside my dad by using this card.

00:15:45.020 --> 00:15:47.650
But the card is gone.

00:15:48.610 --> 00:15:49.520
Kajiki...

00:15:49.520 --> 00:15:52.960
That's why the duel is over!

00:15:55.200 --> 00:15:57.830
Kajiki, so that's how it is?

00:15:59.610 --> 00:16:07.170
That's what your dad and the heavily-scarred Fisherman taught you?

00:16:07.170 --> 00:16:10.250
If your dad can see you now, he'll laugh at you!

00:16:10.250 --> 00:16:11.310
What?

00:16:11.520 --> 00:16:17.140
Duelists like us always fight for something that's in our hearts.

00:16:17.600 --> 00:16:20.250
Your own heart is your opponent!

00:16:20.600 --> 00:16:22.190
My heart...

00:16:22.190 --> 00:16:23.540
That's right.

00:16:23.540 --> 00:16:28.130
Your dad sent you The Legendary Fisherman in order to fight your heart.

00:16:28.360 --> 00:16:34.130
But you're acting like a spoiled kid who's hoping to find his dad in that card.

00:16:35.280 --> 00:16:36.500
Dad!

00:16:37.980 --> 00:16:39.140
Dad!

00:16:41.370 --> 00:16:44.180
Ryota, surpass me.

00:16:47.620 --> 00:16:49.370
Here I go, Jonouchi!

00:16:49.370 --> 00:16:51.100
Fortress Whale attacks!

00:16:51.100 --> 00:16:53.220
Whale Bombard!

00:16:54.620 --> 00:16:58.060
I activate the trap card Kunai with Chain!

00:17:01.230 --> 00:17:03.500
Jump, Panther Warrior!

00:17:03.930 --> 00:17:08.200
Kunai with Chain increases Panther Warrior's attack points!

00:17:08.200 --> 00:17:12.000
Fortress Whale is still stronger!

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:13.740
You're done, Jonouchi!

00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:15.730
No.  Here I go, Kajiki!

00:17:15.730 --> 00:17:18.500
Panther Warrior, counterattack Fortress Whale!

00:17:19.410 --> 00:17:20.290
What?

00:17:23.060 --> 00:17:25.260
Too bad, Jonouchi.

00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:30.420
Panther Warrior battled Fortress Whale, which has greater attack points.

00:17:30.880 --> 00:17:33.090
Panther Warrior is destroyed!

00:17:33.420 --> 00:17:38.800
It's true that Panther Warrior has fewer attack points than Fortress Whale.

00:17:38.800 --> 00:17:41.540
But I still have a set card!

00:17:41.730 --> 00:17:42.840
A set card?

00:17:43.100 --> 00:17:44.560
Here I go, Kajiki!

00:17:44.560 --> 00:17:47.770
This is my trump card, Lightning Blade!

00:17:49.450 --> 00:17:52.280
It gains 800 attack points!

00:17:57.070 --> 00:17:59.150
Fortress Whale is sunk!

00:18:02.490 --> 00:18:03.580
All right!

00:18:03.580 --> 00:18:04.680
Way to go!

00:18:06.760 --> 00:18:08.220
How's that, Kajiki?

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:12.300
Jonouchi, my turn isn't over yet.

00:18:12.650 --> 00:18:15.770
I play the spell card Return of the Doomed.

00:18:15.770 --> 00:18:18.900
It resurrects the monster that was destroyed this turn.

00:18:19.060 --> 00:18:20.840
That means...

00:18:21.400 --> 00:18:24.580
Fortress Whale will return.

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:25.780
It's all over.

00:18:26.160 --> 00:18:27.400
My turn.

00:18:28.790 --> 00:18:29.450
I draw.

00:18:30.100 --> 00:18:35.450
Giant Trunade... This card sends all spell and trap cards on the field back to the hand.

00:18:35.680 --> 00:18:39.160
It can get rid of Kajiki's Umi field.

00:18:39.480 --> 00:18:45.030
But if Fortress Whale is hiding in the waters, Panther Warrior won't survive against it.

00:18:47.270 --> 00:18:49.730
What's up?  Come at me!

00:18:49.730 --> 00:18:54.470
You talk a big game, so show me how you fight!

00:18:55.220 --> 00:18:58.200
I can't afford to lose either.

00:18:58.200 --> 00:19:01.450
There's a battle that I want to fight.

00:19:01.450 --> 00:19:03.350
I won't give up!

00:19:05.540 --> 00:19:07.090
I activate a spell card!

00:19:07.820 --> 00:19:09.220
Giant Trunade!

00:19:16.900 --> 00:19:17.760
What?

00:19:18.020 --> 00:19:22.200
I'm not willing to leave this card in the graveyard.

00:19:24.300 --> 00:19:25.720
I have no regrets!

00:19:25.720 --> 00:19:27.210
Bring it, Jonouchi!

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:30.140
I summon Scapegoat.

00:19:31.850 --> 00:19:34.050
I tribute one of them.

00:19:36.220 --> 00:19:38.250
Panther Warrior attacks!

00:20:01.000 --> 00:20:04.010
Well done, Jonouchi.  I lose.

00:20:04.340 --> 00:20:05.340
Kajiki...

00:20:06.180 --> 00:20:07.680
The rules are the rules.

00:20:09.470 --> 00:20:12.850
No way!  I can't take that card!

00:20:12.850 --> 00:20:15.550
I want you to have this card.

00:20:15.760 --> 00:20:19.760
If I keep it, I'll rely on it too much.

00:20:20.100 --> 00:20:23.230
If you take it, I know I can change.

00:20:23.230 --> 00:20:24.450
Kajiki...

00:20:27.850 --> 00:20:31.270
I'll treasure this card!

00:20:31.830 --> 00:20:33.060
You better!

00:20:33.330 --> 00:20:35.360
I'll win next time!

00:20:35.360 --> 00:20:37.280
I'll be stronger too!

00:20:51.480 --> 00:20:52.850
Understood.

00:20:52.850 --> 00:20:55.700
We found your friend.

00:20:56.200 --> 00:20:57.360
Thanks, Kaiba.

00:20:58.460 --> 00:21:00.030
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:21:00.030 --> 00:21:02.960
I don't care about that amateur.

00:21:02.960 --> 00:21:06.300
I just want to get your Egyptian God Card.

00:21:06.800 --> 00:21:09.310
Kaiba, I'll tell you this.

00:21:09.850 --> 00:21:12.480
Jonouchi is now a great duelist.

00:21:13.100 --> 00:21:14.650
I won't let you insult him.

00:21:14.900 --> 00:21:19.120
I promised to duel Jonouchi in Battle City.

00:21:19.360 --> 00:21:22.360
A serious match between two duelists.

00:21:23.060 --> 00:21:26.990
Follow me if you want to save your friend.

00:21:40.130 --> 00:21:43.630
Bakura, what happened?  You're seriously hurt!

00:21:43.630 --> 00:21:48.830
Namu, who rescued Bakura, asks Jonouchi to teach him how to duel.

00:21:48.830 --> 00:21:52.660
But the Ghouls capture us!

00:21:52.660 --> 00:21:59.800
As we're held hostage, the Rare Hunters Lumis and Umbra challenge Yugi and Kaiba to a duel.

00:21:59.800 --> 00:22:03.230
It's a life-and-death duel on the roof of a skyscraper!

00:22:03.700 --> 00:22:07.160
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Curse of the Mask
Skyscraper Duel

00:22:07.160 --> 00:22:08.730
Duel, standby!

00:22:22.560 --> 00:22:27.070
Even a long, long time ago

00:22:27.860 --> 00:22:32.440
I feel like I've been here

00:22:32.960 --> 00:22:42.090
The setting sun colors the classroom after school

00:22:42.400 --> 00:22:53.600
We all laugh as you point out that I cut my bangs too short

00:22:56.490 --> 00:23:01.130
Time passes bit by bit

00:23:01.790 --> 00:23:06.410
The time when my bangs touch my eyelids

00:23:06.960 --> 00:23:11.510
Will never change

00:23:12.170 --> 00:23:16.780
The sunset envelops everyone

00:23:17.410 --> 00:23:21.990
To be who I am

00:23:22.580 --> 00:23:27.230
I've kept searching for something

00:23:27.880 --> 00:23:31.930
The time that we're now spending together

00:23:31.930 --> 00:23:34.870
I learned that's the answer

00:23:35.660 --> 00:23:41.940
From now until forever...
